WEBVTT

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:11.900
To be able to invite so many guests from the Federation and be together at this banquet

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:15.620
fills me with endless joy.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:21.000
Then, in celebration of prosperity of Gallia, cheers.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.710
Cheers!

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.000
No, not that!

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.540
What reason are you here for?

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.380
Oh, right.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:33.050
If you glare like so, I have no choice but to answer.

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:39.390
A word of advice: if you don't want to get yourself in trouble, you should return soon.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:41.720
Relay this to the young ones.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:48.310
A court lady will be here shortly to assist you with your return.

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:49.440
Understood.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:53.360
I need to return to the banquet.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:00.370
Who is it?!

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.620
Chapter 12

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.620
Kidnapped Princess

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.890
'Till we meet again. Good night.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:38.070
You too, Baron. Let's meet again at the opera.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:42.560
General Jaeger, sir.

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:50.990
A person resembling Princess Cordelia was taken away in the direction of Schladen Roadway just now.

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:52.740
As expected.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:55.370
However, there is something that bothers me, sir.

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:56.280
What is it?

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:59.620
There was someone other than Princess Cordelia who was kidnapped.

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:01.050
Someone else?

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:02.290
Was it the lady-in-waiting?

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:05.600
No, sir. She was wearing a dress, so she couldn't be.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:07.840
What's going on?

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:09.000
Well...

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:25.850
Faldio.

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:30.070
The guests have left the castle.

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:31.070
Is that so?

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:31.940
Hm?

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.490
What about Alicia?

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:36.450
Wasn't she with you?

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:39.660
She said she was going to get you.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:41.930
We haven't seen her.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:46.170
Faldio?

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:49.170
Huh? What is that?

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.090
It's a ragnite crystal.

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:53.220
It was on the floor here.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:55.070
Ragnite?

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.640
That ragnite!

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:00.430
You bastards!

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:02.310
Did you do something to Alicia?!

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:04.810
Faldio!

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:24.120
Princess Cordelia?

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:28.290
Yo, what are we going to do about the other one? Do we finish her here?

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:32.210
No, if the corpse was discovered, it would be bad.

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:34.260
We're going to take her all the way to Adowen?

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:36.300
It's going to cost us double.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:40.390
Adowen... It's the town located on the border with the Federation.

00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:42.260
Why...?

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:43.930
We'll take them back by car.

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:48.900
I don't know about the descendent of Valkyria thing,

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:51.690
but if she's asleep, she's as human as we are.

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:52.980
You said it.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:02.410
That other person Carl saw was probably your friend.

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:10.540
You say that, but is it not the Empire who schemed all this?

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:13.630
What do we gain from abducting the Princess?

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:16.840
We'll just give the Feds a good thing to bite on.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:19.220
To protect Gallia and what-not.

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:25.220
There is probably someone who wants power even if it meant selling Gallia to the Feds.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:38.530
When morning comes, defection of the Princess to the Federation will be known.

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:45.790
In respect to that matter, the Federation has no relation. It was all done by will of the Princess herself.

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:54.920
After this, Gallia will become the Federation's protectorate.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:56.460
When that time arrives...

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:57.920
Of course.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:05.680
When the time comes we'll put you, who has wielded power as the Prime Minister in charge of Gallia.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:11.650
Even so, why Alicia?

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:14.570
There is no reason for them to take her.

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:18.110
Something unexpected must have happened.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:20.650
She was accidentally there, maybe.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:26.330
Let us go, General.

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:28.790
There is no time for us to be involved with this.

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:30.000
Please wait.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.920
Won't you lend us a hand?

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:35.170
I think we can cooperate.

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:39.510
Welkin!

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:41.050
They are our enemies!

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:42.760
They are Imperials!

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:44.390
I know that.

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:46.180
But that doesn't matter right now.

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:50.310
What do you mean, Lieutenant Gunther?

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:55.230
If you cooperate, we will be able to rescue Princess Cordelia and Alicia,

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:58.230
and the Empire can stop Gallia from becoming part of the Federation.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:03.880
This could be seen as a positive symbiosis where both of us will benefit.

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:11.500
Symbiosis, huh?

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:13.040
What an interesting thought.

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:17.000
I see.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:20.550
So Gallia has a lot of assignments to solve.

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:27.050
Thank you very much.

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:29.890
Lieutenant Gunther!

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:32.020
Miss Ellet.

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:34.980
What did you talk about with those guests just now?

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:36.190
Eh?

00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:38.820
You know who they are.

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:46.950
Lieutenant Gunther, Schladen Roadway seems to be the shortest way to get to the Federation,

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:52.040
but considering the time needed to get over the mountain pass, Roben Roadway will take less time.

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:54.960
That's what it seems like.

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:59.290
We can take the Roben Roadway, and you can take Schladen.

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:00.090
Over.

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:02.630
We took some time to start.

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:04.720
We can't catch up with them anytime soon.

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:06.430
Oh, we will.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:13.980
To me, it seems like you just jumbled the situation up.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.940
I want to know if he is for real.

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:19.310
For real?

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:20.230
Yeah.

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:25.360
Whether he is the opponent that can stand up to us or not.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.710
Schladen Roadway...

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:37.750
Welkin!

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:39.920
Get on!

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:40.500
Okay.

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:43.100
Let's go, Faldio.

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:45.340
Welkin.

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:47.510
Failure is unacceptable in this plan.

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:51.970
It is a situation that can swing the fate of this very nation.

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:56.520
We don't know if Alicia is really with Princess Cordelia or not.

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:06.740
Searching for Princess Cordelia means searching for Alicia, and saving Alicia means saving Princess Cordelia.

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:08.740
I think of this like that.

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:12.160
I got you.

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:18.580
You're the leader of this mission, Lieutenant Gunther.

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:25.590
Let's get going as well.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:30.470
Okay. Thanks.

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:32.140
I'll hang up now.

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:34.390
What's going on?

00:08:34.390 --> 00:08:37.230
There is no information from anywhere.

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:39.940
Was I tricked?

00:08:40.980 --> 00:08:44.780
Roger. That is something that you can't tell me.

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:45.690
Yeah.

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:49.910
Well, fine. You may go.

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:51.780
Thank you, Miss Ellet.

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:53.870
But just one thing.

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:59.460
In respect to this case, would it be okay for me to say "do your best?"

00:09:01.460 --> 00:09:02.500
Of course.

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:04.420
That's not it.

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:10.930
What I can think of now is an incident that is waiting to be revealed.

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:18.270
That's a Federation's...

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:23.560
Princess?

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:24.560
Princess!

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:27.070
This place is...

00:09:27.070 --> 00:09:30.360
Are you all right, Princess?

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:32.110
You are...

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:37.660
I am Gallian Militia 3rd Regiment's Sergeant Alicia Melchiott.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:39.250
Militia?

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:43.920
It looks like we have been abducted and are being taken to the Federation.

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:46.800
We must escape from here somehow.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:48.100
But how?

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:49.840
Probably...

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:55.680
No. I'm certain my comrades will come to aid us, so it'll be fine.

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:57.760
There is no need.

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:01.980
It is fine whatever happens to me.

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:03.900
You may escape by yourself.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:05.230
Huh?!

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:06.190
What?

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:07.270
Did you say anything?

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:08.480
No.

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:09.990
Take a look at the back.

00:10:09.990 --> 00:10:11.610
Maybe they've awaken.

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:18.660
Nah. Seems like they are sleeping well together.

00:10:20.410 --> 00:10:23.580
Princess, why do you say that?

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:34.430
If they have changed to a car, then wouldn't we have lost our lead?

00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:38.350
Ramal, how many cars have we seen up to now?

00:10:38.350 --> 00:10:39.430
Eh?

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:42.730
Two or three, sir?

00:10:42.730 --> 00:10:44.060
That's right.

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:46.190
Not only that, but they were all headed in the other direction.

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:51.610
Hence, it means the car that is headed in the direction of the border is the suspicious one.

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:57.910
Hey, Ramal.

00:10:57.910 --> 00:10:58.700
Yes, sir?

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:01.910
Where is this country headed?

00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:08.130
The military is in a factional feud, and the leader is nearly non-existent.

00:11:08.130 --> 00:11:10.140
Ministers who do things as they wish.

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:12.920
Wouldn't they may as well be theives?

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:15.050
That is...

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:18.470
Commander, over there!

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:20.810
Give Welkin the location.

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:21.640
Yes, sir!

00:11:22.850 --> 00:11:24.850
Understood. Don't overdo it.

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:28.440
We will catch up via Edelweiss as soon as possible.

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:30.190
We are going to take a shortcut.

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:32.110
Take care not to bite your tongue.

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:43.040
Hey.

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:51.880
Faldio!

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:53.090
Take this!

00:12:01.390 --> 00:12:02.560
I'll leave her up to you.

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:03.180
Yes, sir!

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:13.070
Damn it!

00:12:16.570 --> 00:12:17.780
Faldio!

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:35.380
Princess Cordelia!

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:36.880
Alicia!

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:38.170
Welkin!

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:40.430
Make a leap over here!

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:43.810
Got it.

00:12:43.810 --> 00:12:44.970
Come, Princess!

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:47.310
Go ahead by yourself.

00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:52.940
Even if I go back, nothing is going to change.

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:55.280
Borg will take care of everything.

00:12:56.860 --> 00:13:01.910
What do you plan to write on Princess Cordelia's letter of departure?

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:07.870
It will read, "After listening to Ambassador Townsend's speech, my admiration for the Federation grew."

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:09.330
That is swell.

00:13:12.380 --> 00:13:13.790
Letter of departure?

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:15.880
What do they mean?

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:19.630
Hence, it's fine with me.

00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:23.930
Knock it off already!

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:29.270
Do you think everyone is born where they want to be and live how they want to live?

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:34.770
It seems you're thinking that nothing will change, but have you ever done anything up to now?

00:13:35.270 --> 00:13:38.070
Go! Trust Welkin!

00:13:39.070 --> 00:13:41.700
Hurry!

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:44.450
Alicia!

00:13:44.450 --> 00:13:45.490
Look out!

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:48.660
Stay put!

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:49.540
Alicia!

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:52.210
Hey! Don't you make a move too!

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:55.180
You try anything stupid, and I'll shoot this kid!

00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:08.100
You're late.

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:10.100
Is the guest unharmed?

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:13.520
When you say "guest," do you mean a princess?

00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:15.860
What are you talking about?

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:21.360
Unfortunately, the one we brought is not a princess,

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:25.780
but a witch.

00:14:30.830 --> 00:14:32.540
Yeah. This is going well.

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:36.750
Welkin, take the Princess!

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:39.130
Shut up! Do you wanna die?!

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:45.010
Stop!

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:46.390
What are you going to do if you hit Alicia?

00:14:46.390 --> 00:14:47.180
Don't move!

00:14:47.180 --> 00:14:50.010
Hey, do you not care about what's going to happen to this girl?

00:14:57.860 --> 00:14:59.610
Welkin, stop!

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:00.440
Hey, hey!

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:01.610
Shoot him!

00:15:08.070 --> 00:15:10.080
Princess Cordelia, quickly!

00:15:10.620 --> 00:15:12.330
Come! Jump!

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:14.870
Yes!

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:16.330
Shit!

00:15:19.670 --> 00:15:21.550
Go!

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:35.060
Damn it!

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:56.000
Thanks.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:57.760
Alicia! Faldio!

00:15:58.170 --> 00:16:00.420
Are both of you okay?

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:02.250
No. I'm not okay at all.

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:03.630
Huh? Are you injured?

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:04.670
Nope.

00:16:04.670 --> 00:16:06.380
Look at this!

00:16:06.380 --> 00:16:10.470
I dirtied the dress I borrowed from Susie this much.

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:12.100
That's it?

00:16:12.100 --> 00:16:13.430
Hold it!

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:16.390
You just thought "Is that all?" or something, right?

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:19.940
Um, no. That's not what it is...

00:16:19.940 --> 00:16:22.110
Then what exactly is it?

00:16:22.110 --> 00:16:24.860
Well, that is...

00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:25.740
Welkin.

00:16:26.570 --> 00:16:27.950
Let's return to the castle,

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:29.660
before the sun rises.

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:33.700
Is that so? That's great.

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:38.040
It is difficult for a country that has become a tributary to gain independence again.

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:42.880
The flow of history is inevitable, but you don't want to leave a regret...

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:44.750
like I have.

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:47.420
I'll see you then, Lieutenant Gunther.

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:50.590
Let me say this to you while I am still your friend.

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:53.470
You did well.

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:05.170
As Lieutenant Gunther has stated, I think that I will not release this incident to the public.

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:12.030
Whoever may have planned this, I do not want to give my people unneeded feeling of insecurity.

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:15.090
That is a wise decision.

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:22.000
Does that mean everything will be unchanged and unchanging?

00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:28.340
To me, I still need the help of many people.

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:33.600
We rescued the Princess, but it didn't do much.

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:38.020
Sergeant Melchiott.

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:39.350
Miss Ellet.

00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:41.440
What about the Princess?

00:17:43.440 --> 00:17:44.650
Really?

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:50.780
Well, if you guys decided not to make it public, then I can't write an article on it.

00:17:50.780 --> 00:17:52.410
Miss Ellet...

00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:54.450
I'm fine,

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:56.160
but take care.

00:17:57.080 --> 00:18:01.710
You might have just drawn an overwhelming joker.

00:18:02.670 --> 00:18:04.170
Joker?

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:06.130
Borg?

00:18:06.130 --> 00:18:08.250
You will lend me your strength as you have, right?

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:11.050
Yes, of course, Your Majesty.

00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:13.760
Lieutenant Gunther.

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:14.840
Yes, Your Majesty.

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:18.140
Please give these words to Sergeant Melchiott.

00:18:18.640 --> 00:18:26.750
Without your words and trust of Lieutenant Gunther, I would not have been here.

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:28.230
Yes, Your Majesty.

00:18:28.230 --> 00:18:29.730
I shall deliver them to her.

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:37.830
How were you able to shoot?

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:38.790
Eh?

00:18:39.290 --> 00:18:41.910
When Alicia was taken hostage.

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:47.290
Ah. It was because I thought protecting Princess Cordelia was the priority.

00:18:47.290 --> 00:18:51.380
You didn't think "What if anything happened to Alicia?"

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:52.880
That's right.

00:18:52.880 --> 00:18:54.930
I didn't think about it.

00:18:54.930 --> 00:18:56.050
Why was that?

00:18:56.720 --> 00:18:59.060
Trust, huh?

00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:05.350
I don't quite understand either, but it was fine if it were Alicia or something...

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:12.780
I can't put it in words well, but it was all so abrupt that I didn't have it in mind.

00:19:14.490 --> 00:19:16.070
Ah, right.

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:17.820
This.

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:20.600
You gave this to Alicia, right?

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:21.730
Yeah.

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:26.400
If this wasn't on the floor, we would have not realized that Alicia was missing.

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:28.080
You saved us.

00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:31.080
Saved us, huh?

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:31.990
Yup.

00:19:33.090 --> 00:19:34.050
Welkin.

00:19:34.050 --> 00:19:34.990
Hm?

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:39.470
Your words sometimes sound extremely arrogant.

00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:42.750
What do you mean, arrogant?

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:49.160
If I told you that I loved Alicia, then what would you do?

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:14.190
My name is Berthold Gregor.

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:20.950
People have dubbed me "the Devil," but a nickname that really suits me is "the Punisher."

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:28.100
We must wipe all of the Darcsens out, and all people should kneel before the glory of His Highness, the Emperor.

00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:34.140
